{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling: the application test-kit design in baa75642 is not accepted\n\nHugh's bar, 4 November 08:00 EST: accept a test suggestion only if it can be radically simplified and still gives a worthwhile guarantee.\n\nThe design proposes a four-stage test kit: a plan representation, typed handles, boundary strategies, negative pairs, command histories, schedules, shrinking, impact selection and coverage reports. Each stage adds a surface that authors and dap must maintain, and most of its guarantees are partial by its own account: finite exploration, guards that may be unreachable, and generated cases that cannot show the author chose the right guard. No single stage gives a guarantee that is both strong and small.\n\nSo I file nothing from it. The assessment stays on record as advice for request 52392bb2; the checker ratifies its own report.\n\nOne finding is small and real: the generic Ledger in packages/derive/test/fixtures.ts grants every actor every declared action by default, so a wrong-actor scenario can pass for authorization reasons rather than business ones. I name it for Hugh to decide; it is not filed.\n\nAny later proposal in this area starts from one guarantee an author can state in a sentence, with the smallest mechanism that delivers it, and asks Hugh before it becomes a request.","body":{"to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d16f726c9d30ea22ff7eaf7db3634e80"}}